"""Prepared reference solution for FlagGems ``nuclear_norm``.

Candidate ABI (frozen Definition ``definitions/nuclear_norm.json``,
``aten::nuclear_norm(Tensor self, bool keepdim=False) -> Tensor``):

* input:  ``self`` = tensor with 2 or more dims, ``keepdim`` bool (default False)
* output: sum of the singular values over the last two dims; shape ``(*,)`` when
  ``keepdim`` is False and ``(*, 1, 1)`` when it is True
* effects: ``mutates: []``, ``returns_alias_of: {}`` -- the result is a new
  tensor, it keeps the input dtype/device, and the input is not written.

The oracle is the same one the frozen master correctness suite uses
(``torch.linalg.matrix_norm(..., ord="nuc")``), so the wrapper adds no
tolerance, dtype, layout or device adaptation.  ``flag_gems`` is not imported
and ``flag_gems.nuclear_norm`` is never called, so the injected candidate is not
used as its own oracle.  FlagGems does register ``aten::linalg_matrix_norm``,
but this file runs with gems dispatch disabled (the suites call the
``flag_gems.*`` export directly and the benchmark resolves the ``--override``
callable instead of ``use_gems``), and even under gems dispatch the
``linalg_matrix_norm`` implementation computes ``ord="nuc"`` through its own
``_svdvals_for_norm`` path rather than calling ``nuclear_norm``.
"""

import torch


def run(self, keepdim=False):
    """Return the nuclear norm of ``self`` (sum of its singular values)."""
    return torch.linalg.matrix_norm(self, ord="nuc", keepdim=keepdim)
